      "name": "PiDP11IOExpander",
      "notes": [
        "2 polygon pours imported as editable Atrium pours (outline, net, pour order, island removal). Clearance and connect style come from the design rules.",
        "2 pours set Altium's Remove Necks option, which Atrium does not model; a repour keeps narrow necks.",
        "5 stored polygon fill region(s) kept as the pours' current copper. They count for connectivity until a repour regenerates them.",
        "19 free region(s) imported as filled shapes (Bottom 1, Silk 18).",
        "Kept 1 net class (signals and tags).",
        "Omitted 4 other class(es) (component, pad, layer, polygon).",
        "Omitted embeddedfonts6 (1).",
        "Omitted advanced placer options6 (1).",
        "Omitted design rule checker options6 (1).",
        "Omitted componentbodies6 (23).",
        "Omitted pin swap options6 (1).",
        "Omitted widestrings6 (65).",
        "Omitted shapebasedregions6 (24).",
        "Omitted shapebasedcomponentbodies6 (23).",
        "Omitted fileversioninfo (1).",
        "Omitted models (12).",
        "Omitted unionnames (1).",
        "Omitted boardregions (1).",
        "Omitted uniqueidprimitiveinformation (100).",
        "Omitted primitiveparameters (46).",
        "Omitted waivedviolations (15).",
        "Omitted layerkindmapping (1).",
        "Omitted constraintmanager (1).",
        "Tessellated arcs (3).",
        "Layer-specific pad stacks simplified (32).",
        "PCB import projects 2D geometry. Layer-specific pad stacks, pours and manufacturing settings require review in the source design."
      ],
